# Design System Constraints (Liquid Glass / calm / ADHD-friendly)

- Dark theme, never pure #000. Base is near-black blue.
- Every new animation MUST be gated by reduced-motion: if enabled → duration 0 OR a fade ≤150ms. Never leave a hard cut.
- Never animate View width/height/blur; use transform/opacity. For SVG shape attrs (width/x/strokeDashoffset) direct animation is OK.
- Max 1 live BlurView per screen. Never blur behind data/text, never inside list items.
- Glow budget: max 1 glowing element per screen, shadowOpacity ≤ 0.32.
- Press feedback: scale to 0.975 minimum (never deeper), entrance ≤120ms, spring release with damping ≥ 16. Label opacity never below 0.92.
- Haptics: ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light on press/select; NotificationFeedbackType.Success ONLY when completing an action. Nothing on scroll.
- No confetti, no particle bursts, no infinite loops (a breathing orb runs ONE cycle on mount, then rests).
- Data viz language: pill/capsule shapes (borderRadius 999 or rx=half-height), monotone cubic curves (NEVER polyline, never overshooting curves), area gradient 0.16→0, only ONE active dot visible.
- Interactive states must differ by SHAPE too (dot/ring/check), not color alone. Must survive grayscale.
- Contrast measured on WORST-case background. Lavender text/strokes use #A9ADFF. Text on lavender fills uses #14152A.
- Touch targets ≥ 44pt.
- No new dependencies unless the task lists them explicitly.
- After every task run: cd mobile && npx tsc --noEmit — FAIL the task if any error appears that is NOT already in tsc.baseline.txt.
- Minimal diffs: never reformat, rename, or refactor code outside the task scope.
